\"515.1\" cy=\"132.1\" r=\"3.5\" fill=\"#C9A84C\" stroke=\"#20242C\" stroke-width=\"1\"/></svg></figure>\n<p>These lines are mine, not yours.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Trend:</strong> Last close $610.05, above the 20-day ($595.88), 50-day ($550.83) and 200-day ($564.46). The 50-day is still under the 200-day.</li><li><strong>Momentum:</strong> RSI 58.3. Neither stretched nor washed out.</li><li><strong>Ceiling:</strong> $657.00, the Oct 30 swing high. Above that, the 52-week high $683.27 (Mar 2).</li><li><strong>Floor:</strong> $595.88 first (38.2% pullback, the same price as the 20-day by coincidence), then $577.00, then $558.12 with the 200-day at $564.46. The Nov 6 low of $561.85 held just above that zone.</li><li><strong>Your tested edge:</strong> Does not apply. The 50-day is below the 200-day and RSI is not under 40.</li><li><strong>Plays:</strong> None open or watching on LMT.</li><li><strong>Verdict:</strong> The chart supports the upside, modestly. Price fell from $643.15 to $567.08 in four sessions, held the deepest pullback line, and has closed higher three days running. A daily close below $558.12 flips it to the downside. The chart agrees with what management described.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-would-change-this-read\">What would change this read</h3>\n<ul><li>Dec 11: the stopgap ends. A full-year bill helps; another stopgap or a shutdown hurts.</li><li>A signed F-35 Lot 20 contract, or a filing that puts a dollar figure on the gap.</li><li>Next report: date not found. January brings 2027 guidance.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"confidence-and-sources\">Confidence and sources</h3>\n<p>Solid: release figures (read twice in the source doc). Medium: call details, from a machine transcript with visible errors. Thin: the dividend rate (transcript only), production rates, 10-Q text (not opened), the year of the independent-chair vote.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://news.lockheedmartin.com/2026-10-22-Lockheed-Martin-Reports-Third-Quarter-2026-Financial-Results\" target=\"_bla